  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technological and enterprise upgrading programme on agro-chemicals and agricultural machinery production sector (Industrial upgrading and modernization in Cuba, phase II)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The pilot project #Technological and enterprise upgrading programme on agro-chemicals and agricultural machinery production sector (Industrial upgrading and modernization in Cuba)# (ID 150262) spanned during the period of 6 years (2016-2022). According to the #Sectoral Strategy for the technological and enterprise upgrading of fertilizers and agricultural machinery# that was developed during the initial stages of implementation, taking into account the eventual amount of mobilized funding (USD 2,000,000 - 50% of the initially envisaged budget), it was recommended that the technical assistance during the project#s pilot phase should only focus on reinforcing production capacities of the agro-chemicals/fertilizer industry in Cuba. As a result of the project, two pilot fertilizer plants were upgraded (CIIQ #Revoluci&#x106;&#xb3;n de Octubre# fertilizers manufacturing plant in Havana and EMPREQUIN in Nuevitas), ensuring the necessary fine-tuning within the production process of calcium nitrate, while also promoting innovative liquid fertilizer CBFERT/VITAPLIC Foliar.  In April 2023, in an official letter of the Ministry of Foreign Trade and Foreign Investment addressed to UNIDO, the pilot international cooperation project in Cuba was acknowledged for its significant impact on agricultural development and food sovereignty in th</narrative>
  </description>
